; Split-horizon RPZ for Unbound on arawi, applied only to clients tagged "lan"
; (the DNS Resolver custom options). Unbound applies a qname trigger to the
; name a client asks for and to every CNAME target while resolving, so
; nextcloud.regulad.xyz -> ingress.regulad.xyz is rewritten too. A passthru
; (CNAME rpz-passthru.) ends RPZ processing for the whole query, its CNAME
; targets included, so a name with one gets its public records even where its
; target has a rule of its own.
;
; Owners are relative to the zone origin: "ingress.regulad.xyz" here triggers
; on ingress.regulad.xyz. Only the name itself matches; "*.<name>" would match
; its subdomains.
;
; The master copy lives at /usr/local/etc/unbound/split-horizon.rpz; Unbound
; reads the copy in its chroot, /var/unbound/split-horizon.rpz, which
; /usr/local/bin/unbound-rpz-restore.sh recreates at every boot.
$ORIGIN split-horizon.rpz.
$TTL 60
@ IN SOA localhost. nobody.invalid. 1 3600 600 86400 60
@ IN NS localhost.

ingress.regulad.xyz IN CNAME ingress.regulad.internal.
dodo.regulad.xyz IN CNAME dodo.regulad.internal.
mail.regulad.xyz IN CNAME mail.pubsub.wahlecloud.oraclevcn.com.
livekit.regulad.xyz IN CNAME livekit.pubsub.wahlecloud.oraclevcn.com.

; Public records, through ingress.regulad.xyz's public ones: aboriginal's
; Nextcloud fetches RSSHub's feeds, and refuses a name with any internal
; address unless allow_local_remote_servers lets every fetch reach one.
rsshub.regulad.xyz IN CNAME rpz-passthru.
